From: Gucioo <7483436+Gucioo@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fanctl: fix positional option name containing a space

fanctl fails on every invocation, including `fanctl get` and
`fanctl status`:

    fanctl failed: Invalid positional Name: fan list

CLI11 validates option names when the option is added, and rejects a
positional name containing a space. Because the whole command tree is
built before any argument parsing happens, the exception is thrown during
construction and no subcommand can ever run. The tool is unusable as
shipped.

Rename the positional to fan_list. Positional names are only used in help
and error text, never typed on the command line, so this does not change
how fanctl is invoked.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/control/fanctl.cpp	2026-09-06 11:14:21.102931648 +0000
+++ b/control/fanctl.cpp	2026-09-06 11:14:21.102931648 +0000
@@ -901,7 +901,7 @@
     cmdSet->set_help_flag("-h, --help", strHelp);
     cmdSet->add_option("target", target, "RPM/PWM target to set the fans");
     cmdSet->add_option(
-        "fan list", fanList,
+        "fan_list", fanList,
         "[optional] list of 1+ fans to set target RPM/PWM (default: all)");
     cmdSet->require_option();
 
